.SH "NAME"
pcre2_substring_number_from_name \- convert captured string name to number
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

int\fP \f(CBpcre2_substring_number_from_name\fP\f(CR(const pcre2_code *\fP\f(CIcode\fP\f(CR,
                                     PCRE2_SPTR\fP \f(CIstringname\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This convenience function finds the number of a named substring capturing
parenthesis in a compiled pattern, provided that it is a unique name. The
function arguments are:
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 11
\f(CIcode\fP
.ad l
Compiled regular expression
.TP 11
\f(CIstringname\fP
.ad l
Name whose number is required
.PD
.RE
.PP
.ad l
.sp
The yield of the function is the number of the parenthesis if the name is
found, or \f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING\fP if it is not found. When duplicate names are
allowed (\f(CBPCRE2_DUPNAMES\fP is set), if the name is not unique,
\f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_NOUNIQUESUBSTRING\fP is returned. You can obtain the list of numbers
with the same name by calling \f(CBpcre2_substring_nametable_scan()\fP.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.